{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rrnewton/hermit/pulls/3054","id":4555537410,"node_id":"PR_kwDOIZiOrM8AAAABD4f8Ag","html_url":"https://github.com/rrnewton/hermit/pull/3054","diff_url":"https://github.com/rrnewton/hermit/pull/3054.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/rrnewton/hermit/pull/3054.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rrnewton/hermit/issues/3054","number":3054,"state":"closed","locked":false,"title":"Preserve guest randomness across SaBRe startup","user":{"login":"rrnewton","id":274582,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI3NDU4Mg==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/274582?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/rrnewton","html_url":"https://github.com/rrnewton","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rrnewton/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rrnewton/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rrnewton/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rrnewton/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rrnewton/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rrnewton/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rrnewton/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rrnewton/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rrnewton/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"[hermit2, degraded-dev-hermit, gpt-6-astra, devbig014, role=impl]\n\n## Plain Language Summary and Project Impact\n\nPreserve guest randomness across SaBRe startup so real programs reach and satisfy Hermit's existing parity and record/replay checks. SaBRe consumes entropy before Detcore starts; this change authenticates that startup state, transfers it once to the real root thread, and keeps plugin-internal getrandom calls out of the guest's libc state.\n\n## Summary\n\nThe supervisor binds bootstrap evidence to the owned process generation, image, configuration, held object bytes and loader phase. Initial state transfer, kernel-observed later exec continuation and supported initial static dispatch have distinct typed results. Wrapper frames and SIGILL/UD0 stops retain separate proofs. Raw Unix paths and process names remain opaque bytes. Large image snapshots use bounded copying into anonymous read-only file-backed storage; 128 MiB selects storage rather than rejecting an image. Cleanup stays with the owned child lifecycle.\n\nThe reader authenticates the actual trusted loader representation: final argv bytes/order/NULs against the kernel exec-stop capture and held shebang prefix, executable entry/site anchors for duplicate interpreter mappings, and copied program headers only at the exact authenticated address with the loader's one-page anonymous geometry, permissions and original bytes. Malformed, mismatched and ambiguous evidence still refuses.\n\nPlugin-domain libc getrandom calls now use the raw native syscall; guest-domain calls retain the original libc call-through and its exact result/errno semantics. The matching producer installs these detours before plugin statistics/path/signal initialization. The installer stages the actual bundled Cargo-built loader and licenses and verifies its single-line revision contract.\n\nThis advances Hermit's Cargo dependency references and lockfiles to already-landed Reverie `30fee360d6359e38a429f6bf19d30cdfac9c1d0d`, carrying [the producer repair](https://github.com/rrnewton/reverie/pull/575). The complete incoming range also includes the independently landed LiteInst owned-signal-frame change `56881777ee0e107708a5a829ba9ba535c6bb61c9`; SaBRe controls do not certify that backend's parity.\n\nFinal candidate: `c0ca7a0666245ce0d71e8e9ca6ba338f2fa22452`, tree `c2f810e62c101415e9b0c106c97fe38060d78144`; includes actual Hermit main `421e08cefb8a6dd84ffc0fcf4a7bcbf5f64803bd`.\n\n## Determinism\n\nEarly guest requests use Detcore's Pcg64Mcg implementation, including flags, draw consumption and partial-memory-fault behavior. Authenticated state is consumed once into a virgin root, without replacing ThreadState or importing clocks/scheduler state. Initial auxv completion is recorded once without another draw. Exec continuation carries no RNG state and requires the owned EXEC event. Missing or stale proof cannot create a replacement stream.\n\nPlugin entropy is deliberately native and separate from guest accounting. This does not establish complete early syscall/clock accounting, static/later-exec vDSO coverage or universal backend parity.\n\n## Linux Semantics\n\nObject proof retains the held FD/device/inode, root-relative no-follow path, complete original bytes, frame/instruction identity and process generation. vDSO absence requires maps/auxv agreement. Guest libc forwarding and rewritten syscall routing remain distinct. Private-prctl collisions refuse; intervening events can invalidate saved SIGILL proof. Existing static admission and parser behavior are retained.\n\nLarge snapshots still require supported backing and available resources; repeated authentication has a cost. Loader registration uses the initial caller/loader TLS pair, not an arbitrary-thread API. The producer reviews retain nonblocking limitations for nearby detour extents, protection-failure handling, reentrancy and prefix matching; this consumer does not claim those are fixed.\n\n## Validation\n\nAt final c0ca, formatting, workspace all-target/all-feature Clippy, actual discovery of all 674 unit identities and the original six SaBRe identities, and the normal nine-node constructed-DAG export passed. The 97.463-second scope completed with 4.52 GiB peak memory and zero recorded memory/PID-limit events; its source binding matched all 1,728 entries before and after. Discovery does not execute the test bodies. The unchanged callback separately passed its exact guest-forwarding and plugin-isolation/error test in the preceding adoption check.\n\nThe earlier official nine-node selection at `0ad33fe44e8354b882ed0e351d59e99bb96e6779` passed all seven prerequisites/producers, all 671 unit methods, and five of six SaBRe methods. The remaining method reached its original stdout equality assertion and found different getrandom bytes. Its later strict verification was not reached. The full selected run failed in 674.302 seconds; its complete evidence remains retained.\n\nA subsequent private diagnostic with the plugin-domain change and an earlier producer candidate matched one ptrace and two SaBRe outputs. It used a DEBUG CLI and private dependency overrides and supplies no final-head or canonical-full credit. Final producer regression tests passed two methods/eight native loader cases; targeted Clippy and both independent source reviews passed before the actual upstream landing.\n\nThe final-head official driver launched the nine-node focused run at 14:32:52Z from the owned consumer slot. It is explicitly off the record and cannot publish a validation receipt. The off-record diagnostic completed successfully in 681.297 seconds: all seven prerequisites/producers passed, all 674 unit tests passed with none skipped, and all six original SaBRe tests passed with none skipped. The previously failing libc getrandom test passed, including its unchanged stdout/strict-verification requirements. Six BitwiseInfoV1 verification reports and twelve logs are retained. Sampled resource observations recorded no memory/PID-limit events or query gaps; final scopes/cgroups and observed driver/observer generations are gone. This remains diagnostic evidence with no canonical receipt. Detailed report: `/home/newton/work/dev-hermit/ignored/ci-hub/run1828-fix-forward-20260916/consumer-c0ca-focused-result-review-1/REPORT.md`. Full log: `/home/newton/work/dev-hermit/ignored/ci-hub/run1828-fix-forward-20260916/consumer-30fee-official-preparation-1/official-focused-c0ca7a066624-30fee1/FULL.log`.\n\nThe original test assertions, strict comparisons, prepared-executable requirements and node limits remain required. Both independent source reviewers approved exact c0ca: native Codex/GPT-6 Astra and an actual external Claude Opus 5 [1m] invocation (417.091 seconds, zero permission denials). Both exact-head comments were read back and attested. Claude retains the upstream silent-detour-installation risk and notes that the two budget carry ledgers lack a final 30fee paragraph; the unchanged DBT source inputs and bounds are independently established in the adoption evidence. These observations remain visible and are not reported fixed. A full validation at the actual newly landed Hermit main remains a separate obligation; main is not declared green by this PR's source/component evidence.\n\n## Human Review Required\n\nTriggers 2 and 3 apply: syscall-interception/bootstrap abstraction and deterministic initial-state transfer. This follows the owner's post-facto P0 repair policy, with actual independent Codex and Claude reviews bound to the final head. Human review should examine the bootstrap proof boundary, one-time RNG-state import and plugin/guest separation.\n\nTaskGraph: `hermit-main-tip-d0b1468b-not-validated-22-nodes-mostly-exit-2`, owner `dev-hermit`. Final evidence: `/home/newton/work/dev-hermit/ignored/ci-hub/run1828-fix-forward-20260916/consumer-main421-native-1/REPORT.md` and `/home/newton/work/dev-hermit/ignored/ci-hub/run1828-fix-forward-20260916/consumer-final-source-review-1/final-c0ca7a06-1/REVIEW.md`.\n\nLanded as `6bd63ef1740a7680adfd0a6b4585942ec06aa2b8` at 2026-09-17T14:37:28Z. All 24 complete changed files and modes were read back byte-identical on main; the landed tree equals the reviewed/runtime-tested c0ca tree. The first canonical full launch was refused during old-checkout cleanup before any test ran; it is not a full result.\n","created_at":"2026-09-17T06:44:54Z","updated_at":"2026-09-17T14:53:01Z","closed_at":"2026-09-17T14:37:28Z","merged_at":"2026-09-17T14:37:28Z","merge_commit_sha":"6bd63ef1740a7680adfd0a6b4585942ec06aa2b8","assignees":[],"requested_reviewers":[],"requested_teams":[],"labels":[{"id":11603596200,"node_id":"LA_kwDOIZiOrM8AAAACs6DTqA","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rrnewton/hermit/labels/post-facto-human-review","name":"post-facto-human-review","color":"FFA500","default":false,"description":"Landed under post-facto protocol; needs human review","archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":11681812195,"node_id":"LA_kwDOIZiOrM8AAAACuEpO4w","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rrnewton/hermit/labels/adversarial-review-codex1","name":"adversarial-review-codex1","color":"5319e7","default":false,"description":"Codex adversarial review round 1 completed","archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":11681812218,"node_id":"LA_kwDOIZiOrM8AAAACuEpO-g","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rrnewton/hermit/labels/adversarial-review-claude1","name":"adversarial-review-claude1","color":"1D76DB","default":false,"description":"Adversarial review pass, claude lane (round 1)","archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":11684277015,"node_id":"LA_kwDOIZiOrM8AAAACuG_rFw","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rrnewton/hermit/labels/passed-review-claude","name":"passed-review-claude","color":"0E8A16","default":false,"description":"Claude adversarial review PASSED at current PR head","archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":11685076479,"node_id":"LA_kwDOIZiOrM8AAAACuHwd_w","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rrnewton/hermit/labels/passed-review-codex","name":"passed-review-codex","color":"0E8A16","default":false,"description":"Codex adversarial review PASSED at current PR head","archived_at":null,"archived_by":null}],"milestone":null,"draft":false,"commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rrnewton/hermit/pulls/3054/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rrnewton/hermit/pulls/3054/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rrnewton/hermit/pulls/comments{/number}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rrnewton/hermit/issues/3054/comments","statuses_u